  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Use the remainder theorem to find the remainder when $P(x)=x^4-6x^2+3x+2$ is divided by each linear polynomial $D(x)$. Then state whether or not $D(x)$ is a factor of $P(x)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$D(x)=x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remainder $0$; $x-1$ is a factor.",
          "worked": "The remainder is $P(1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1^4-6(1)^2+3(1)+2\\\\P(1)&=1-6+3+2\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nSince the remainder is zero, $x-1$ is a factor of $P(x)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$D(x)=x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remainder $-6$; $x+1$ is not a factor.",
          "worked": "Since $x+1=x-(-1)$, the remainder is $P(-1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=(-1)^4-6(-1)^2+3(-1)+2\\\\P(-1)&=1-6-3+2\\\\P(-1)&=-6\\end{align*}$$\nSince the remainder is nonzero, $x+1$ is not a factor of $P(x)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 41
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$D(x)=x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remainder $38$; $x-3$ is not a factor.",
          "worked": "The remainder is $P(3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(3)&=3^4-6(3)^2+3(3)+2\\\\P(3)&=81-54+9+2\\\\P(3)&=38\\end{align*}$$\nSince the remainder is nonzero, $x-3$ is not a factor of $P(x)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$D(x)=x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remainder $20$; $x+3$ is not a factor.",
          "worked": "Since $x+3=x-(-3)$, the remainder is $P(-3)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-3)&=(-3)^4-6(-3)^2+3(-3)+2\\\\P(-3)&=81-54-9+2\\\\P(-3)&=20\\end{align*}$$\nSince the remainder is nonzero, $x+3$ is not a factor of $P(x)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 41
      }
    ]
